{comment}
  A bare page: one column of plain type, monochrome, light or dark as the visitor's system is set. Nothing else --
  no header, footer, navigation or search, no JavaScript at all, and none of the partials base.html.dtmpl adds to
  every page (analytics, experiments, personalization, the consent banner, chat). Its first use is a landing page
  ("Under construction"), assigned to a whole site; any page may use it.

  The head keeps the SEO partial (title, description, canonical), so an indexable site is described as any other.
  The styles are inline: one small block, no theme stylesheet, so nothing else is fetched.
{endcomment}<!doctype html>
<html lang="{var:content.locale default=`en`}">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
    {include:`partials/seo-head.html.dtmpl`}
    <style>
        :root { --bare-fg: #111; --bare-muted: #555; --bare-bg: #fff; }
        @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
            :root { --bare-fg: #eee; --bare-muted: #aaa; --bare-bg: #111; }
        }
        html, body { margin: 0; background: var(--bare-bg); color: var(--bare-fg); }
        body {
            font: 1.125rem/1.6 system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
            min-height: 100vh; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
        }
        main { max-width: 36rem; padding: 2rem 1.5rem; }
        h1 { font-size: 2.25rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.01em; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
        p { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
        a { color: inherit; text-underline-offset: 0.2em; }
        .bare-muted { color: var(--bare-muted); }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <main>
        {slot:content}{endslot}
    </main>
</body>
</html>
